    "The script runs a custom wrapper script, `../set_affinity_gpu_polaris.sh`, which suggests GPU usage and affinity settings are required. However, no GPUs are requested in the job directives. The job will fail if the wrapper script attempts to access or bind to GPUs that have not been allocated. A directive such as '#FLUX --gpus-per-task=1' should be added.",
    "The script sets up and starts a Postgres database on the lead node of the job allocation. This database is then accessed by all 40 MPI ranks. The database server commands (`initdb`, `pg_ctl`, `createdb`, `dropdb`) are executed without `flux run`, meaning they will only run on the single lead node. This is correct, but it creates a potential single-node bottleneck and a single point of failure for the entire job."
  ]
